import hashlib
import json
from pathlib import Path
import shutil

app=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];root=app.parent
identifier='EN-20261110-02';directory=root/'docs/research-journal/evidence'/identifier
directory.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=False)
sources={
 'security-tests.log':app/'.artifacts/d1-runtime-lab/google-activation-security-tests-20261110.log',
 'live-browser-and-callback.json':app/'.artifacts/d1-runtime-lab/google-live-final-20261110/result.json',
 'login-desktop.png':app/'.artifacts/d1-runtime-lab/google-live-final-20261110/login-desktop.png',
 'login-mobile.png':app/'.artifacts/d1-runtime-lab/google-live-final-20261110/login-mobile.png',
 'google-desktop.png':app/'.artifacts/d1-runtime-lab/google-live-final-20261110/google-desktop.png',
 'google-mobile.png':app/'.artifacts/d1-runtime-lab/google-live-final-20261110/google-mobile.png',
}
for name,source in sources.items():shutil.copyfile(source,directory/name)
report='''# Google sign-in activation

Observed 2026-11-10 Asia/Saigon. The user supplied a protected Web OAuth JSON and authorized server secret configuration and login testing. A local helper validated Web type, project and exact callback, streamed the two Google credential values directly to Wrangler stdin, and returned uploaded:true without copying credentials or printing values. The original ACL was not changed. git check-ignore confirms the supplied .cache file is excluded. No credential JSON or secret value is included in these evidence files.

Worker version7b84648b-b99a-4632-8011-71363795a21a, fresh instanceenglish-google-20261110-v1. The existing verified D1/private recording image was reused with --containers-rollout none. Server status now enabled:true, anonymous connected:false. Secret-name inventory contains both Google keys and no legacy Neon/Blob credentials. Website persistence stays on Cloudflare. No source reset/seed, user password change or real-user impersonation was performed.

Executed node --test tests/google-auth.test.cjs tests/auth-cookie.test.cjs:15PASS exit0 in isolated data. Public/live browser script exit0: desktop and mobile show Google/password controls, no horizontal overflow/runtime errors, and reach Google's account sign-in page without invalid_client or redirect_uri_mismatch. Actual live callback probes verify exact callback, PKCE S256, basic identity scopes, secure HttpOnly state cookie, forged-state rejection, cancellation and consumed-state replay rejection against D1. These probes create/consume only their own short-lived flow states.

The user permitted skipping unnecessary tester registration, alternatively naming their own account. Google documents an exception for requests limited to basic identity scopes and Sign in with Google: https://support.google.com/cloud/answer/15549945?hl=en . This app requests only openid email profile, as directly checked in the live authorization URL. No tester was added and no audience or publishing setting changed. The user was asked to complete one real login and report the final application outcome. No password, verification code or cookie was requested. Existing matching-email accounts retain the explicit password-login/Settings-link requirement.

Important limit: reaching Google's sign-in form does not verify user consent, code exchange, verified ID token, account linking/creation or final application session. Real login verification is still pending user interaction. Initial combined shell checks and a later multiline documentation shell edit were rejected by automatic review; those commands did not execute. Public checks were separated from credential handling and documentation used structured apply_patch; the safe checks and edits succeeded. First browser summary had a constant passwordAvailable field; the final harness queries/asserts the actual password input and reruns. Earlier raw logs retained privately, not rewritten into historical successes.
'''
(directory/'verification.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
ep=root/'docs/research-journal/evidence.json';e=json.loads(ep.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
number=max(int(item['id'][2:])for item in e['items'])+1;ids=[]
for name in ['verification.md',*sources]:
 file=directory/name;code=f'MB{number}';number+=1;ids.append(code)
 e['items'].insert(0,{'id':code,'path':file.relative_to(root).as_posix(),'scope':'Observed Google server activation, isolated security tests and public browser/callback checks. Actual consent and final user session not yet verified.','inspected_on':'2026-11-10','event_date':'2026-11-10','sha256':hashlib.sha256(file.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})
ep.write_text(json.dumps(e,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
jp=root/'docs/research-journal/journal.json';j=json.loads(jp.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
assert not any(item['id']==identifier for item in j['entries'])
j['entries'].insert(0,{'id':identifier,'kind':'observed','title':'Google sign in enabled with protected server credentials and live browser checks','date':'10/11/2026','stage':'OAuth activation and acceptance','status':'Google enabled; real consent and final application login pending','participants':'User supplied protected Web credentials and authorized testing. Codex configured, deployed and checked. Other participants and location not confirmed.','objective':'Activate the existing Google integration without exposing credentials or changing preserved user data, and verify the live flow as far as authorized account access permits.','equipment':'Wrangler, Cloudflare Worker/Containers/D1, protected Web client JSON, Node/Puppeteer Chrome desktop/mobile, isolated auth/cookie tests, Python/lxml.','procedure':'Validate site project/callback and stream credentials directly to Wrangler. Use a fresh named app instance with the existing image. Run isolated security tests and real public browser/callback checks. Verify secret names and ignore rules. Review Google Testing scope exception; ask for real account consent outcome.','results':'Google enabled on version 7b84648b-b99a-4632-8011-71363795a21a. No credential copy/value output or source ACL change; supplied .cache JSON ignored by Git. 15 isolated tests PASS exit0. Desktop/mobile live browser checks PASS with Google/password controls and Google sign-in page reached. Live PKCE/callback/cookie, forged-state, cancellation and replay checks PASS. Only controlled ephemeral flow states mutated. User allowed skipping unnecessary tester registration; basic identity scope exception applies, so no tester/audience changes performed. Actual consent, token exchange and final user session not yet verified. Automatic review rejected two combined shell operations; safe separated checks and structured edits succeeded.','lessons':'Distinguish provider activation and Google sign-in-page reachability from completed consent and application authentication. Avoid extra credential copies and never treat unrelated CLI login as website credentials. Testing basic identity scopes is exempt from the test-user allowlist.','next':'User completes one real Google login and reports the resulting page or error; verify final authenticated session/link behavior. Preserve source data and keep secrets server-side. Rendering review tracked separately.','evidence':ids})
jp.write_text(json.dumps(j,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
with(root/'docs/WORKLOG.md').open('a',encoding='utf-8')as f:f.write('\n\n## 2026-11-10 — Google sign-in activated (EN-20261110-02)\n\n- Server Google credentials streamed directly from protected Web JSON without copy/value output; fresh instance english-google-20261110-v1, version7b84648b-b99a-4632-8011-71363795a21a. Cloudflare persistence unchanged.\n-15 isolated auth/cookie tests and live desktop/mobile/callback checks PASS; actual consent/token exchange/final app session pending user login. Basic identity scope exemption permits skipping tester allowlist, as user allowed. No tester/audience changes made.\n- Evidence: research-journal/evidence/EN-20261110-02/. Source credential excluded from Git; no real user password or preserved source data altered.\n')
with(app/'deploy/cloudflare/MIGRATION-STATE.md').open('a',encoding='utf-8')as f:f.write('\n\n### 2026-11-10 Google server activation\n\nGoogle credentials validated and streamed from the protected user file directly to Wrangler, no credential copy/value output. Source ACL unchanged and source cache ignored by Git. Current status enabled:true; fresh instance/version listed above.15 isolated tests and live desktop/mobile/callback checks PASS, including actual D1 cancellation and state replay rejection. Existing D1/media image reused. Real user consent/code exchange/final session remains unverified; user asked to perform one login. Google basic identity scope exemption means no test-user allowlist entry is required; user allowed skipping it, so no tester or audience changes were made. See EN-20261110-02 and GOOGLE-AUTH.md.\n')
print(json.dumps({'entry':identifier,'evidence':ids,'google':'enabled','realLogin':'pending'}))
